inuous plan, surrounded by pale sand-colored ground and sparse native grasses. Warm sunset light enters from the upper right, casting long, soft-edged shadows across warm wood floors, bamboo screens, linen upholstery, and muted earthy surfaces. At the top center, clean dark-brown sans-serif lettering reads \"JAPANDI RESIDENCE\". The open-plan layout is divided by low timber partitions and sliding shoji-style screens into clearly legible rooms labeled \"ENTRY\", \"LIVING\", \"DINING\", \"KITCHEN\", \"STUDY\", \"BEDROOMS\", \"BATH\", and \"TERRACE\". In the lower left, the entry hall contains a woven rush mat, a cedar console table, two ceramic vessels, and a recessed coat niche. Beside it, the living room holds a low oatmeal-colored sofa facing a rectangular walnut coffee table on a natural jute rug, with two rounded lounge chairs, a bamboo pendant lamp, linen curtains, and a sculptural branch arrangement in a clay vase. The dining area occupies the center-left, furnished with a long oval oak table, eight simple spindle-back chairs, and a shallow stone bowl beneath a circular paper lantern. Along the upper center, the kitchen has matte limewashed walls, pale veined marble counters, flat-front oak cabinetry, open shelves with neutral ceramics, a broad island with three stools, and a compact sink beneath a window. On the right, the study contains a built-in desk, reading chair, shelving, and stacked books. Two bedrooms sit along the lower right, each furnished with a low platform bed, rumpled beige bedding, timber headboards, bedside tables, and woven rugs; between them, the bathroom combines pale limestone flooring, a freestanding oval tub, a floating oak vanity, folded towels, and a bamboo shower screen. Wide sliding doors connect the central rooms to a covered terrace lined with timber posts, bamboo fencing, potted olive trees, and a rectangular reflecting pool. Thin dimension lines, wall thicknesses, door swings, stairs, and furniture remain crisp and readable throughout the plan, while the empty rooms contain no people."], "inputs": [{"shape": 7, "name": "anything", "link": 13, "label": "输入任何", "type": "*", "localized_name": "anything"}], "flags": {}, "id": 13, "type": "easy showAnything", "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "easy showAnything"}, "order": 15}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "*", "links": [13, 24, 49], "label": "输出", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "*"}], "size": [270, 78], "pos": [1524.6802978515625, 502.6833801269531], "widgets_values": [true], "inputs": [{"name": "tt_value", "link": 23, "label": "真", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "tt_value"}, {"name": "ff_value", "link": 21, "label": "假", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "ff_value"}, {"widget": {"name": "cond"}, "name": "cond", "label": "条件", "type": "BOOLEAN", "localized_name": "cond"}], "flags": {}, "id": 20, "type": "ImpactConditionalBranch", "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "ImpactConditionalBranch"}, "order": 14}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "output", "links": [], "type": "*", "localized_name": "output"}], "size": [488.106201171875, 268.902099609375], "pos": [1523.6634521484375, 636.98291015625], "widgets_values": ["Photorealistic 3D architectural visualization of a Japandi residential house interior, shown from a high bird’s-eye view as an orthographic cutaway floor plan with the roof removed. The wide composition presents the entire single-story home and its distinct functional zones within one continuous plan, surrounded by pale sand-colored ground and sparse native grasses. Warm sunset light enters from the upper right, casting long, soft-edged shadows across warm wood floors, bamboo screens, linen upholstery, and muted earthy surfaces. At the top center, clean dark-brown sans-serif lettering reads \"JAPANDI RESIDENCE\". The open-plan layout is divided by low timber partitions and sliding shoji-style screens into clearly legible rooms labeled \"ENTRY\", \"LIVING\", \"